{
  "description": "Coldcard dice-only seed math. Each case was produced by Coldcard's own rolls.py (24 words) and rolls12.py (12 words) run offline, and matches an independent standard-library computation. The 123456 case is Coldcard's published example. Test data only; never use these seeds. Provenance: vectors/SOURCES.md.",
  "math": "E = SHA256(ASCII(rolls)). words_24 = BIP39 encoding of all 32 bytes of E (8-bit checksum = first byte of SHA256(E)). words_12 = BIP39 encoding of the first 16 bytes of E (4-bit checksum = top nibble of SHA256(E[0:16])). English BIP39 word list.",
  "newline": "rolls is the digits only. Both scripts read one line with input().strip(), so the trailing newline from echo, a CR and any surrounding whitespace are never hashed, and anything after the first line is ignored. SHA256(\"123456\\n\") would be e150a1ec81e8e93e1eae2c3a77e66ec6dbd6a3b460f89c1d08aecf422ee401a0.",
